OL,3,GNEWSAFamily's terror over mistaken HMO
OL,4,Agang attack
OL,5,
OL,6,FA father has told of his family's
OL,7,Fterror after their home was mistakenly
OL,8,Fattacked by a balaclava-wearing gang
OL,9,Fopposed to Houses of Multiple Occupancy
OL,10,F(HMOs).
OL,12,FBlack graffiti reading: "No HMOs, No,
OL,13,FNo" was daubed over the house in Little
OL,14,FHulton, Salford, and a brick was
OL,15,Fsmashed threw through their living room
OL,16,Fwindow on 13 October.
OL,18,FThe family's two sons, aged four and
OL,19,Ftwo, were asleep upstairs at the time.
OL,20,FTheir father said: "We want to get out
OL,21,Fof here. It feels unsafe."
OL,23,APub: 20-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NW Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
FL,409,400,260,160,0,100
